# Sprint 3: Shift Management Implementation

This plan outlines the implementation of Shift Management for the CoffeePOS system. This connects the cashier workflow with transaction tracking to ensure accurate daily financial reconciliation.

## Open Questions

> [!NOTE]
> Database Migration: I will create a `Back-End/migration-sprint3.sql` file. Please confirm if you will run this manually in your Supabase dashboard or if you have an automated migration tool.
> Note about `pos.ts` API: When inserting a transaction, we need to associate it with the `shift_id`. The backend will use `req.user.id` to look up the active shift, so the frontend doesn't need to manually send `shift_id`. Please confirm this approach.

## Proposed Changes

---

### Backend: Database & API

#### [NEW] `Back-End/migration-sprint3.sql`
- Creates `coffeepos.shifts` table.
- Alters `coffeepos.transactions` to add `shift_id` and `cashier_id`.
- Creates necessary indexes for performance.

#### [NEW] `Back-End/src/routes/shifts.ts`
- **POST `/shifts/open`**: Validates no active shift exists, then creates a new shift.
- **POST `/shifts/close`**: Calculates expected cash from transactions, compares with actual cash, updates shift status, and calculates totals.
- **GET `/shifts/active`**: Fetches the current active shift for the logged-in cashier.
- **GET `/shifts`**: (Owner only) Paginated list of all shifts with filters.
- **GET `/shifts/:id`**: (Owner only) Details of a specific shift including its transactions.

#### [MODIFY] `Back-End/src/app.ts`
- Register the new `/shifts` router with `authenticateToken` middleware.

#### [MODIFY] `Back-End/src/routes/pos.ts`
- Update the `/pos/checkout` endpoint to automatically attach the `shift_id` to new transactions if the user is a cashier and has an active shift.

---

### Frontend: Context & UI Components

#### [NEW] `Front-End/src/contexts/ShiftContext.tsx`
- Creates `ShiftContext` to manage `activeShift`, `isLoading`, `openShift`, `closeShift`, and `refreshShift`.
- Automatically fetches active shift on mount if the user is a cashier.

#### [MODIFY] `Front-End/src/main.tsx`
- Wraps the `<App />` component with `<ShiftProvider>` inside the `<AuthContext>` so it has access to the user token.

#### [NEW] `Front-End/src/components/shift/ShiftOpenModal.tsx`
- Modal that forces the cashier to enter the opening cash amount before starting their shift.

#### [NEW] `Front-End/src/components/shift/ShiftCloseModal.tsx`
- Modal to close the shift, displaying total sales, expected cash, and allowing the cashier to input actual cash. Displays the variance (selisih) in real-time.

---

### Frontend: Integration & Gates

#### [MODIFY] `Front-End/src/components/Layout/Sidebar.tsx`
- Adds a "Tutup Shift" button and a "Shift Aktif" / "Belum Buka Shift" status badge for cashiers.

#### [MODIFY] `Front-End/src/pages/Dashboard/CashierDashboard.tsx`
- Implements the shift gate. Triggers `ShiftOpenModal` if there is no active shift.

#### [MODIFY] `Front-End/src/pages/PointOfSale/index.tsx` & `Front-End/src/pages/Operation/WasteLog/index.tsx`
- Adds a check to prevent cashiers from accessing POS or Waste Log if they don't have an active shift.

#### [MODIFY] `Front-End/src/components/operation/WasteLogTable.tsx`
- Restricts editing and deleting waste logs for cashiers (hides the buttons).

---

### Frontend: Owner Reporting

#### [NEW] `Front-End/src/pages/Shifts/index.tsx`
- Owner dashboard for shift reports. Displays summary metrics and a paginated data table.

#### [NEW] `Front-End/src/pages/Shifts/detail.tsx`
- Detailed view of a specific shift, including a breakdown of all transactions that occurred during that shift.

#### [MODIFY] `Front-End/src/data/navigation.ts` & `Front-End/src/App.tsx`
- Adds the new Shift Laporan routes for owners.

## Verification Plan

### Automated/Manual Verification
- Run the SQL migration in the database.
- Start backend and frontend servers.
- **Cashier Flow**: Login as cashier -> Verify `ShiftOpenModal` appears -> Open shift -> Verify POS is accessible -> Close shift -> Verify logout.
- **Owner Flow**: Login as owner -> Go to Shift Report -> Verify shift details are recorded correctly.
- **Waste Log Flow**: Login as cashier -> Verify Edit/Delete buttons are hidden.
